# Dual Git remotes (mandatory)

This repository has **dual-git enabled**. Any time you push (commit, branch,
release, or tag) you MUST update **both** remotes in the same turn — do **not**
wait for the user to say "dual-git" or "mirror to Azure".

- `origin`: `https://github.com/ahmadubuntu/mongodb_administration.git`
- `azure`: `https://azure.charisma.tech/DataPlatform/DataPlatform/_git/mongodb_administration`

Keep `main` tracking `origin/main`.

## Every push checklist

1. `git push origin <branch>` (and tags if any)
2. Push the same refs to `azure` with `AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM` (never `AZDO_PAT`)
3. `git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main` if upstream drifted
4. If Azure is unreachable, say so explicitly and leave the exact retry commands

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git push origin main
git push origin --tags   # when tags changed
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure main
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure --tags
git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main
```

Never print, commit, or embed the PAT in a remote URL.

Read-only check:

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" ls-remote azure
```

## Inventory secrets

Real cluster inventories (`mongodb_realtime_check/config/clusters/*.env`) are
gitignored. Only `*.example.env` may be committed.
